# script_chapter6.rpy
#
# Chapter 6. Another group class with Silvia.

image cg_eyes = "cg eyes.png"

label chapter_six:

    nvl clear 
    scene bg studio day

    cn "I continued attending one class with Silvia every Sunday afternoon. 
    \nEach time I could feel my confidence grow a little more. 
    \nThe breathwork and yoga built in complexity each time, 
    but it became a familiar challenge." 

    cn "Light chatter with my classmates became easier. \nI felt more like I belonged there, like I was one of them."

    cn "I still hadn't exchanged more than a few words with Silvia. She seemed untouchable, perfect."

    cn "After a few standard yoga sessions, I felt ready to try one of her more intense courses."

    scene bg studio night
    play sound "pad_low.mp3" volume 0.7

    show ana default with easeinleft:
        xpos 30
        ypos 60

    n "For this evening class, the yoga studio had moody, ambient lighting. There were some familiar faces, and some unfamiliar ones. I unfurled my mat and chatted with the women next to me about the traffic, the weather, all the usual light stuff."

    show silvia default with easeinright:
        xpos 500
        ypos 10

    n "Silvia soon emerged, breezing over to the center of the room." 
    
    n "Her clothes always looked so loose and comfortable, but are cinched in just the right places to show off her incredible figure."

    n "She pressed her hands together, and greeted the room."

    nvl clear 

    show silvia default at hop

    s "Good evening ladies!"

    s "You made a wise choice coming out tonight. We're going to dig deep with this one."

    s "Don't be scared, I'll be right here with you the entire time."

    s "Let's start in a circle, with some sitting poses, to open up your heart-space."

    play music "amoebic_sea.mp3" fadein 4 

    n "I felt nervousness growing in my chest for whatever came after this. "

    nvl clear 

    n "Silvia guided us through a handful of seated stretches, and had us breathe slowly, slowlyyyy."

    s "It's so important to learn to commune with your shadow self when you work on self improvement."

    s "The shadow is everything about our inner self that we hate, that we feel anxious about, that we don't want to admit."

    s "Humans want to distance themselves from their shadows, to hide them away. But it is vital that you don't do this. 
    You must accept yourself as the whole of who you are, including your shadow. "

    nvl clear

    s "I want you to tell the group something you've never told anyone before. 
    Something you're ashamed of."

    n "Mmmm. Okay."

    s "Think of that thing you're ashamed of. Hold it in your head."

    s "Cup your hands like this, in front of you. And picture holding that memory in your open hands. "

    n "In my peripheral vision, I saw the other women in the circle around me extend their cupped hands. 
    I extended my own. "

    s "I know you may feel some resistance in your soul when I say this. But I want you to share 
    the memory with the group. "

    n "Ah, fuck."

    s "This is about embracing your shadow, embracing all that you are. Being vulnerable. 
    Learning to trust."

    nvl clear

    s "I will share first."

    s "When I was in college, I drank. I know that much is not out of the ordinary."

    s "But I drank in excess, in a way that lowered my vibration. "
    
    s "I thought I was being wild and free, but really, 
    I was chasing false idols at the bottom of a bottle. My schoolwork suffered, my friends suffered. I continued, 
    shunning anyone who tried to stop me. "

    nvl clear

    s "I was at a New Years party with my best friend. We went way back, you know? She was my ride or die." 

    s "We were both trashed, and I was trying to get her to finish her bottle of whiskey by the stroke of midnight. 
    She was pushing it away, laughing."

    s "In the push-and-pull, our heels got tangled — "

    nvl clear
    
    s "She fell, and I heard her head hit the kitchen counter with a crack."

    s "The clock struck midnight as I stared at the blood starting to gush over her face. 
    The party around us cheered, unaware."

    n "She paused, staring into the distance with her hands clasped painfully tightly. "

    s "That change in energy, right at midnight, set it into motion for me. "
    
    s "This wasn't the path the universe intended for me. Something needed to change. "

    s "After midnight, it was all a blur." 
    
    s "She went to the hospital. I went back to classes."

    s "She was put on medical leave with a concussion, and I didn't see her for the rest of that semester."

    nvl clear

    s "That was the beginning of my spiritual journey. "
    
    s "I could not bear what I had seen, could not bear to be the kind 
    of person who would do what I did."

    s "So I listened to the universe. I haven't had a single drink since that night."
    
    s "And through yoga, breathwork, and movement, I was remade into the person you see before you now."

    nvl clear

    n "There was a heavy silence after Silvia finished speaking. The class seemed to be processing what she had said."

    n "I... never would've expected that from her. "
    
    n "I guess she really is human. She's right about being a new  person — it's hard to imagine her that messy. 
    She always seems so absolutely in control."

    s "Thank you all for sharing that space with me. "

    n "She turned to the woman on her right."

    s "Would you mind trusting us with your own shadow?"

    nvl clear

    n "The woman nodded hesitantly. "

    n "And around the room it went, with everyone sharing their shameful secrets. The confessions were met with a 
    low murmur of acknowledgement from the listeners, and sympathetic nods."

    n "One woman confessed about how she spoke badly about her mother behind her back for years, and felt 
    immense guilt over it."
    
    n "One told the room that she cheated on her last boyfriend, but he never caught her. "
    
    n "Another talked about how she lost a pregnancy just a week ago. She seemed shattered." 
    
    n "Listening to her, I felt tears well in my eyes — 
    looking around, I was not the only one."

    nvl clear

    n "Sylvia sat tall, gazing at each secret-teller with intense empathy."

    n "I... guess I owe them all this. They brought their own stuff to the table. But I really don't want to talk about 
    it..."

    n "I took a shaky breath and spoke."

    show ana default at hop

    a "W-when I was in high school, there was this girl I really didn't like. I thought she was rich, spoiled, stuck up. "

    a "She was one of my sister's friends, so I couldn't get away from her."

    nvl clear

    a "We all went to the pool together one day." 
    
    a "Me, my sister, and her other friends were all swimming around, but this girl 
    just wanted to lay on the deck chair."
    
    a "She said she didn't like water and she just wanted to tan. We were teasing her about it." 
    
    a "I thought she was acting that way because she was too good for us." 
    
    a "So I went up behind her, picked her up, and threw her in. "

    a "Everyone was laughing with me, I felt so good for a moment. "
    
    a "But she didn't come up for one second, "
    
    a "and then another, "

    a "and then when she did come up she kept flailing her arms and going back under." 
    
    a "My sister stopped laughing immediately and  started lifting her up, pushing her towards the side of the pool, 
    but the girl was weighing her down and pulling her under too." 
    
    a "The other friends joined in and managed to get her to the side of the pool, coughing up water and sputtering and 
    terrified." 
    
    a "I just stood there."

    a "She couldn't swim. She was too embarrassed to tell us, she couldn't swim. "

    a "I was so ashamed." 
    
    a "I didn't want to hurt her, I just thought she was being snotty. But I 
    had no idea. I couldn't bring myself to talk to her after that."

    n "I had been looking down at my cupped hands while I talked." 
    
    n "I looked up at the crowd, and saw the same 
    sympathetic nods as I'd seen for the other speakers. "

    nvl clear

    show cg_eyes with dissolve

    n "Sylvia looked straight at me with intense kindness. It felt like her eyes were piercing into me, 
    seeing behind my skin into my soul, absolving me."

    hide cg_eyes with dissolve

    n "Only a couple people shared after me, and honestly I was too distracted to fully hear what they said. "

    n "Once everyone was finished, Sylvia guided us to release our shame, opening up our hands and lifting them towards 
    the ceiling. "

    n "I felt rattled, but lighter." 
    
    n "These women had heard my shame and hadn't thrown me out, I must really be one of 
    them now."

    n "The air in the classroom after the session ended was solemn and quiet."

    nvl clear

    n "As I turned to head out the door, I felt a tap on the shoulder."

    play music raw fadein 0.5

    show silvia default at hop
    s "Ana, may I speak to you for a minute?"

    n "Shit. Was I in trouble or something? My mind raced and I felt my face start to go red."

    s "Your share today was so brave. I can tell you have a beautiful soul. Thank you for being here today."

    show ana default at hop
    a "A-ah! Thank you, Silvia. That means a lot, coming from you."

    nvl clear

    s "I want to offer you a slot for one of my special one-on-one shadow work classes, 
    I can see that you have the immense strength it takes to do that kind of deep work." 
    
    s "And I think you're at a 
    critical moment in your journey - of course I wouldn't charge you for the session."

    a "Oh!"
    
    a "You really think that about me?"

    s "Of course, love."

    n "I felt my face grow hot."

    a "Thank you....that's so kind of you."

    nvl clear

    n "Suddenly unsure of what to do with my hands, I fidgeted with my hair, twirling it around my fingers. "

    a "I guess...yes, I would like to! How could I say no?"

    s "Perfect, perfect. We can meet here next Saturday at noon. I look forward to seeing you."

    a "I'll see you then!"

    nvl clear 
    stop music fadeout 2

call chapter_seven from _call_chapter_seven
            